{=============================================================================
  Turbojet with component efficiencies (exercise)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0226
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Teaching example (ULiège MECA0002). Station-by-station ideal-gas turbojet:
  inlet diffuser, compressor, combustor, turbine and nozzle. Cold-side and
  hot-side specific heats and gamma are constant. Compressor and turbine
  isentropic efficiencies are given; the shaft balance uses eta_m.
  Specific thrust and specific fuel consumption follow from the nozzle-exit
  velocity. Temperatures stay in kelvin (T_amb = -40+273, T0[4] = 1200+273).
  The original comments out pi_c = 12; the stored solution pi_c = 20 is the
  only equation added.

  Inputs : p_amb, T_amb, c_0, T0[4], pi_c, pi_b, eta_c, eta_t, eta_m,
           C_p_c, C_p_t, gamma_c, gamma_t, PCI
  Outputs: Fs, Cs, f, w_c, w_t, c_7
  Units  : SI - temperatures in K, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : ULiège MECA0002, S. Quoilin - see README.md
=============================================================================}

"!Data"
fluid$ = 'Air' "working fluid = air treated as a perfect gas, as in the original"
p_amb = 22e3 [Pa] "22 kPa in the original"
T_amb = -40+273 "ambient static temperature [K]"
c_0 = 800/3.6 "flight speed, 800 km/h as in the original [m/s]"

T0[4] = 1200+273 "turbine inlet total temperature [K]"
eta_c = 0.85 "compressor isentropic efficiency [-]"
eta_t = 0.88 "turbine isentropic efficiency [-]"
pi_c = 20 "compressor pressure ratio [-]; the original comments pi_c = 12, and the stored solution is 20"
pi_b = 0.97 "pressure ratio across the combustion chamber [-]"
eta_m = 0.99 "as in the original [-]"

C_p_c = 1005 [J/kg-K] "cold-side specific heat, before the combustor (1.005 kJ/kg-K in the original)"
C_p_t = 1140 [J/kg-K] "hot-side specific heat, after the combustor (1.140 kJ/kg-K in the original)"
gamma_c = 1.4 "cold-side ratio of specific heats [-]"
gamma_t = 1.333 "hot-side ratio of specific heats [-]"
R = 287 [J/kg-K] "perfect-gas constant of air (0.287 kJ/kg-K in the original)"
PCI = 43.1e6 [J/kg] "kerosene lower heating value (43.1e3 kJ/kg in the original)"

"!Solution"
"The original solves the cycle from inlet station 1 to exit station 6, computing each component exit from its inlet and the heat and mechanical power exchanged."
"Each component is an open system in steady flow. Kinetic and potential energy changes are neglected, except where the original says otherwise."
"The aircraft speed is not neglected: it produces a ram compression, so the cycle is written with total quantities."

"!Total conditions at the diffuser inlet: station 1"
T[1] = T_amb "static temperature [K]"
T0[1] = T[1] + c_0^2/(2*C_p_c) "total temperature [K]; c_0^2/2000/C_p_c in the original (Cp in kJ/kg-K)"
p[1] = p_amb "static pressure [Pa]"
p0[1] = p[1] * (T0[1]/T[1])^(gamma_c/(gamma_c-1)) "total pressure [Pa]"

"!Diffuser exit / compressor inlet: station 2"
T0[2] = T0[1] "first law, as in the original [K]"
"The original states an isentropic diffuser: with T0[2] = T0[1] the total pressure is conserved."
p0[2] = p0[1] "total pressure [Pa]"

"!Compressor exit: station 3"
p0[3] = p0[2]*pi_c "total pressure [Pa]"
eta_c * (T0[3]/T0[2]-1.0) = pi_c^((gamma_c-1)/gamma_c) - 1.0 "compressor isentropic efficiency [-]"
w_c = c_p_c * (T0[3]-T0[2]) "compressor specific work [J/kg]"

"!Combustor exit: station 4"
p0[4] = pi_b*p0[3] "total pressure [Pa]"
(1+f) * c_p_t*T0[4] = c_p_c * T0[3] + q_b "first law on the combustor, per unit air mass flow [J/kg]"
q_b = PCI * f "f is the fuel-air mass ratio [-]; q_b [J/kg of air]"

"!Turbine exit: station 5"
w_t*eta_m + w_c = 0 "shaft balance: the turbine drives the compressor [J/kg]"
w_t = c_p_t * (T0[5]-T0[4]) "turbine specific work [J/kg]"
eta_t * (pi_t^((gamma_t-1)/gamma_t) - 1) = (T0[5]/T0[4]-1) "turbine isentropic efficiency [-]"
p0[5] = pi_t * p0[4] "total pressure [Pa]"

"!Nozzle exit: station 7"
T0[7] = T0[5] "total temperature [K]"
"The original states an isentropic nozzle: with the total temperatures equal, the total pressure is conserved."
p0[7] = p0[5] "total pressure [Pa]"
"The nozzle converts gas enthalpy into kinetic energy. The original assumes a complete expansion, so the static pressure at the nozzle exit equals the ambient pressure."
p[7] = p_amb "static pressure [Pa]"
T[7]/T0[7] = (p[7]/p0[7])^((gamma_t-1)/gamma_t) "isentropic static temperature at the nozzle exit [-]"
T0[7] = T[7] + c_7^2/(2*C_p_t) "total temperature [K]; c_7^2/2000/C_p_t in the original (Cp in kJ/kg-K)"

"!Specific thrust from a momentum balance. The original comment writes (1+f)*c_6 - c_0; the equation uses c_7."
Fs = (1+f) * c_7 - c_0 "specific thrust [m/s]"

"!Specific fuel consumption: fuel mass flow over thrust, which is f/Fs per unit air mass flow."
Cs = f/Fs "specific fuel consumption [kg/(N-s)]"
